Executive Summary for Government Stakeholders
Project Overview
The objective of this project was to develop an AI-powered customer churn prediction system for banking institutions. The system predicts customer attrition before it occurs and assigns risk scores to support proactive retention efforts.

Dataset
Total Customers: 10,000

Customer Features: 15+

Target Variable: Customer Churn (Exited)

Methodology
The project applied machine learning techniques including Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, Random Forest, and XGBoost. Feature engineering and explainable AI methods were incorporated to improve performance and transparency.

Key Findings
Approximately 20% of customers churned.

Customer age significantly impacts churn likelihood.

Inactive customers are more likely to leave.

Product ownership strongly influences retention.

Geographic location contributes to churn behavior.

Best Model
XGBoost achieved the highest predictive performance and was selected as the final production model.

Strategic Benefits
Early identification of high-risk customers

Improved customer retention rates

Reduced revenue loss

Data-driven policy formulation

Efficient allocation of retention resources

Recommendations
Deploy predictive churn monitoring systems.

Develop targeted engagement programs.

Increase product adoption through bundled services.

Implement region-specific retention strategies.

Utilize explainable AI for transparent decision-making.

Expected Impact
The proposed system can significantly improve customer retention, enhance revenue stability, and strengthen the long-term competitiveness of banking institutions through proactive churn management.

